{
  "about": "Every sound in the game, made by the browser's own sound maker, not from files. A sound is layers played together. Layer kinds: osc = a tone (wave: sine, triangle, square, sawtooth) whose pitch glides freq.from → freq.to in Hz (curve exp or lin); noise = hiss (color: white is bright, pink is softer, brown is a low rumble). filter shapes a layer: type lowpass (keeps low), highpass (keeps high) or bandpass (keeps a band), sweeping from → to in Hz, q is how narrow the band is. env is the loudness over time: it rises over attack seconds to peak, stays for hold, then dies away over release. at starts the layer later (seconds); repeat makes count copies spread over spread seconds (bubbles, crackles); jitter makes each copy's pitch differ by up to that fraction, so repeats never sound alike. volume sets the whole sound's loudness. priority (1..3): when too many sounds play at once the quietest-priority ones are cut first. cooldown: the shortest time between two plays of the same sound. spatial: comes from where it happens (left, right, far away) instead of straight ahead. alert with duck (0..1): other sounds drop to that level while it plays. A real recorded file can replace any of these later by giving the sound a file name in place of layers.",
  "limits": { "voices": 16 },
